description:
Replace Arc<dyn Any> NextValue with a generic Yield<S> keyed on a new SubjectKind marker trait carrying type Payload. Each consumer's wake type is statically known at the call site; no Any downcast at the API boundary.

Resolves prior open question: tag wake should ship the row through the wake instead of a unit sentinel + re-snapshot under store mutex.

Surface:
  pub trait SubjectKind: Send + Sync + 'static { type Payload: Send + Sync + 'static; }
  pub struct SubjectKey<S: SubjectKind> { id: u64, _s: PhantomData<fn() -> S> }
  pub struct Yield<S: SubjectKind> { key: SubjectKey<S>, lineage: Option<Lineage> }
  impl<S: SubjectKind> EffectKind for Yield<S> { type Response = Result<Arc<S::Payload>, Unsubscribed>; }
  pub struct SubjectRegistry<S: SubjectKind> { ... }
  impl<S: SubjectKind> Store for SubjectRegistry<S> {}
  pub struct YieldBatcher<S: SubjectKind> { ... }

Tag consumer:
  pub struct TagWake; impl SubjectKind for TagWake { type Payload = TagRow; }
  TagWriteBatcher ships Arc<TagRow> through registry.next().
  subscribe_stream's wake arm emits row directly, advances last_idx by 1, skipping the second store-mutex acquisition.

Files:
  - v3/crates/effect_runtime/src/subjects.rs (full rewrite)
  - v3/crates/effect_runtime/src/lib.rs (re-exports drop NextValue, add SubjectKind)
  - v3/crates/pipeline/src/effects.rs (TagWake/TagRow defs, Bag.waiters typed, batcher ships Arc<TagRow>)
  - v3/crates/pipeline/src/ops/tag.rs (subscribe_stream wake-arm + build_tag_ctx)
  - v3/crates/server/src/backend.rs + bin/sprefa-run.rs (registrations)

Phase 2 (this session). Land the Yield primitive end-to-end in effect_runtime so all yield-shaped runtime constructs (parked writes, tag-subscribe, Pending captures) collapse to one mechanism.

Vocabulary (locked 2026-04-26): Yield = op-side suspend; Next = outside-world resume; Unsubscribe = outside-world cancel; Subject = keyed pending entry; SubjectRegistry = store; SubjectKey = id; Unsubscribed = cancel-error variant.

Surface (new file v3/crates/effect_runtime/src/yield_.rs):
  pub struct SubjectKey(pub Uuid);
  pub struct CursorLineage { binding_origin, capture_id, ... }
  pub struct NextValue(Box<dyn Any+Send+Sync>);
  pub struct Unsubscribed;
  pub struct Yield { pub key: SubjectKey, pub lineage: CursorLineage }
  impl EffectKind for Yield { type Response = Result<NextValue, Unsubscribed>; }

  pub struct SubjectRegistry { /* DashMap<SubjectKey, oneshot::Sender<Result<NextValue, Unsubscribed>>> */ }
  impl Store for SubjectRegistry {}
  impl SubjectRegistry {
      pub fn next(&self, key: SubjectKey, value: NextValue);
      pub fn unsubscribe(&self, key: SubjectKey);
      pub fn unsubscribe_lineage(&self, predicate: impl Fn(&CursorLineage) -> bool);
  }

  pub struct YieldBatcher { registry: Arc<SubjectRegistry> }
  impl Batcher<Yield> for YieldBatcher { /* register oneshot, select on (recv, cancel) */ }

Author flow (op-side, natural coroutine code):
  async_stream::stream! {
      while let Some(input) = upstream.next().await {
          yield Arc::from([scan_so_far(input)]);
          match cx.put(Yield { key, lineage }).await {
              Ok(value) => continue,
              Err(Unsubscribed) => break,
          }
      }
  }

Tests (must cover):
  1. roundtrip — Yield then external Next resolves with value
  2. external Unsubscribe — Yield resolves Err(Unsubscribed)
  3. op-side cancel (drop the put future) — Subject entry GC'd, no orphan oneshot
  4. runtime cancel_all — every outstanding Yield resolves Err(Unsubscribed)
  5. lineage-invalidation — unsubscribe_lineage(predicate) drops matching subjects
  6. concurrent Next on same key — first wins, second is no-op (or error per design lock)
  7. registry exposed via store TypeMap from rtctx-typemap card

